---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Theming · alert-notify"
  description="Configure light, dark, and system themes and override alert-notify CSS variables."
  pageTitle="Theming"
>
  <h2>Theme mode</h2>
  <pre class="api"><code>{`toast.config({ theme: "light" }); // default
toast.config({ theme: "system" }); // OS + html.dark / data-theme
toast.config({ theme: "dark" });
toast.config({ richColors: true });`}</code></pre>

  <p>
    With <code>theme: "system"</code> the toaster tracks <code>prefers-color-scheme</code>,
    <code>html.dark</code> / <code>html.light</code>, and <code>html[data-theme]</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>CSS variables</h2>
  <p>
    Override colors on <code>.an-toaster</code> in your stylesheet after the package CSS.
  </p>
  <pre class="api"><code>{`.an-toaster {
  --an-bg: #ffffff;
  --an-fg: #0f172a;
  --an-muted: #475569;
  --an-border: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.1);
  --an-success: #15803d;
  --an-error: #e11d48;
  --an-warning: #b45309;
  --an-info: #1d4ed8;
  --an-success-bg: #ecfdf5;
  --an-error-bg: #fff1f2;
  --an-warning-bg: #fffbeb;
  --an-info-bg: #eff6ff;
}

.an-toaster[data-theme="dark"] {
  --an-bg: #1e293b;
  --an-fg: #f8fafc;
}`}</code></pre>
</DocsLayout>
